cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Digital Twin-Based Stochastic Energy Resilience Modelling of Cape Town Municipal Facilities under Load Shedding"

message: "If you use this repository, its code, or derived materials in your research, please cite this repository and the associated research study."

type: software

authors:
  - given-names: "Kingsley"
    family-names: "Ofori"
    affiliation: "University of Johannesburg, Department of Construction Management and Quantity Surveying"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-5950-0892"

repository-code: "https://github.com/kingsleyofori/research-digital-twin-resilience"

abstract: >
  This repository contains the research code, data-processing procedures,
  stochastic simulation models, resilience calculations, and interactive
  visualisation developed for the study of energy resilience in Cape Town
  municipal facilities under load shedding. The study combines historical
  municipal electricity-use data with historical electricity-disruption
  records within a digital twin-based stochastic modelling framework.

keywords:
  - "digital twin"
  - "energy resilience"
  - "load shedding"
  - "municipal facilities"
  - "building energy"
  - "stochastic modelling"
  - "Cape Town"
  - "South Africa"
  - "PyDeck"
  - "Python"

